second check when the agent reports the goal complete; its adapter is
packages/evaluator. What it judges is Guardian's record of the run and the
evidence Guardian adds from the project; the rubrics are the user's own "done
when" items, plus one of Guardian's about unrequested work; the judge is the
user's Cursor model, with one line of Guardian's telling it not to delegate. ADK's dependencies (pydantic,
google-genai and 15 others, pinned in packages/evaluator/requirements.txt, each
under its own licence) are installed as wheels when the extension is packaged
and are not copied here. ADK's evaluators that call Vertex AI's hosted
evaluation are not used.

Codex's own goal package (its goal extension and goal store at ac54a05,
Apache-2.0) runs unmodified beside Guardian's goal file and DeepSeek
Harness's packages: it is fetched from Codex's repository at build time and
linked into packages/codex-goals, and none of it is copied here. Guardian runs
its tool handlers and tool definitions, its turn accounting and token budget,
its handling of a goal the user changes, and its own decision and prompt for
continuing. Its store holds a copy of the goal, its handlers can refuse a
change, and its "complete" is a status change that judges nothing. What is
adapted: Codex produces its continuation turn in a thread started with Codex's
own test support, whose model endpoint is a local capture server, and Guardian
reads that request back, because only Cursor's stop hook can start the agent's
next turn. A goal is recorded as complete only when Guardian's own checks pass
and Codex's handler and DeepSeek Harness's tool both accept it.
